    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0340" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/5323</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Lithuanian Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Balutis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-19">November 19, 1931</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sib</hi>: Referring to your communication of October
                    24, 1931,<anchor n="23" xml:id="d181-f1"/> concerning the postponement of all
                    payments upon the debts of foreign Governments to the American Government
                    payable during the fiscal year beginning July 1, 1931, and a request for a
                    statement of the attitude of the Lithuanian Government with regard to its
                    acceptance of the President’s Proposal, I have the honor to state that I have
                    been instructed by my Government to inform you that the Lithuanian Government is
                    ready to accept the President’s Proposal, as set forth in his statement of June
                    20, 1931.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">B. K. Balutis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
